## What Steam lists now

[Phantom Blade Zero on Steam](https://store.steampowered.com/app/4115450/Phantom_Blade_Zero/), checked on 8 November 2026, is a released paid game. Steam’s app details give 28 October 2026 and no longer mark it as coming soon. The listing is for Windows. It does not list macOS or Linux.

S-GAME Studio is the developer and S-GAME Publishing is the publisher. The publisher’s site is [pbz.s-game.com](https://pbz.s-game.com/). Newer announcements stay on Steam. The live check under this article links to them, and the [updates page](/updates) lists them with the other watched games. GameNews does not copy those posts. These paragraphs stay as written on 8 November 2026.

## What the publisher says the game is

Steam’s short description says you play as Soul, a warrior with sixty-six days to live, in a Wuxia story with action combat. The longer store text says he was framed for murdering his master, and it describes single-player exploration, martial-arts weapons, and a mix of wuxia and industrial fantasy. Those are the publisher’s claims. GameNews has not played the game, so this page does not grade combat, length, or difficulty.

Steam also lists full controller support and recommends a gamepad. It lists subtitle options, adjustable text size, adjustable difficulty, and custom volume controls. English and Simplified Chinese are marked for full audio. Other listed languages are not given that mark. Confirm the current language list on the store page before you buy.

## The PC requirements on the store page

These figures are copied from Steam’s system requirements on 8 November 2026. They are the store’s targets, including its own frame-rate notes. They are not a GameNews benchmark.

The minimum column lists Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit, an Intel Core i7-8700K or AMD Ryzen 5 3600, 16 GB of memory, a GeForce GTX 1660 6 GB or Radeon RX 5500 XT 8 GB, DirectX 12, and 145 GB of space. Steam’s note on that column says 1080p at 30 FPS with upscaling, and that installation requires an SSD.

The recommended column lists the same operating system, memory, storage, and SSD requirement. It lists an Intel Core i5-10600K or AMD Ryzen 5 5600X, and a GeForce RTX 3060 Ti 8 GB or Radeon RX 6700 XT 12 GB. Steam’s note on that column says 1440p at 60 FPS with upscaling.

Compare your PC with the column for the settings you want, on the store page, in case the listing changes. A minimum line is not a promise of that frame rate on your machine. GameNews does not host the game files, and this page does not quote a price.

## What this page does not claim

This replaces the 15 October 2026 pre-release notes. It is a source check of the released Steam listing, not a hands-on review and not a recommendation to buy. GameNews is not affiliated with S-GAME.
